reports/demos/

# Build artifacts (large binaries)
# §11.4.30/§11.4.10 GAP2 root cause: the entire build/ dir is regenerable derivatives
# (make build / go build ./cmd/...). Ignore wholesale so no compiled binary — and no
# secret baked into one — can ever be re-tracked. Was per-file (api/grpc/unified only),
# which let build/ebook-translator (with an embedded SSH password) get tracked.
/build/
# §11.4.30/§11.4.10: root-anchored compiled binaries (build derivatives of cmd/*).
# These 6 previously carried an embedded SSH-password literal — un-tracked + ignored
# here so a rebuild from scrubbed source produces secret-free, never-tracked artifacts.
# Regenerate via `go build ./cmd/...` / `make build`.
/ebook-translator
/download-model
/test-model
/test-enhanced-conversion
/test-simple-translation
/test_ssh_worker
/model-bridge

# Test outputs
cmd/cli/test_output.epub
# §11.4.30: anchor the prebuilt repo-root 'api-server' binary to the root so the
# bare pattern no longer matches the cmd/api-server/ SOURCE directory (it was
# hiding the package + blocking its tests; the build output is build/api-server).
/api-server
# §11.4.30: anchored repo-root compiled binaries (build artifacts of cmd/*). Root-
# anchored so they never match a source dir/file elsewhere (pkg/hash/, cmd/workable-
# items/, docs/workable_items.db are all unaffected). Regenerate via `go build ./cmd/...`.
/hash
/workable-items
test_output.epub

# Raw QA evidence + docs_chain runtime (regeneratable; §11.4.128/§11.4.106)
qa-results/
.docs_chain/state.json
.docs_chain/*.docs_chain.tmp
# mutation-test residue (§11.4.84) — never track
*.go.backup
*.go.bak
*.bak
*.backup

# §11.4.77 — LLMsVerifier bridge: verified-models SQLite cache is a build derivative
# regenerated out-of-the-box by `model-bridge best-model`/`invoke` (in-process verification
# pipeline from *_API_KEY env keys → verify → SQLite). Never versioned (§11.4.30).
data/
pkg/bridge/data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
